{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":1.0,"text":"One dollar, doubling every day, outgrows all the personal wealth on Earth. Guess how many days it takes? Day zero. One crisp dollar bill on a kitchen table. Day one. It's two dollars, and its owner is already proud. Day ten. It's one thousand twenty-four dollars. Fits in a wallet. Day twenty. Just over a million. It needs the whole house. Day thirty. Over a billion. The street is full of money. Day forty. One point one trillion dollars. That's more than the richest person alive, Elon Musk, at about eight hundred sixty-nine billion. Day forty-eight. Two hundred eighty-one trillion. Just over half the world's personal wealth, about five hundred seventeen trillion dollars. Then, one more doubling. Day forty-nine. Five hundred sixty-three trillion. The dollar is bigger than everyone. Luckily, no real investment doubles every day. Unluckily, that includes yours. Doubling works like a snowball rolling downhill. Every turn, it picks up as much as it already carries, so the last single day added as much as the forty-eight days before it combined. Real money grows slower. At the stock market's long-run average of roughly ten percent a year, the same trip takes around three hundred fifty years. So, the answer was forty-nine days, or three hundred fifty years, if you want to keep the dollar.","words":[{"text":"One","start":0.14,"end":0.3,"type":"word","logprob":-0.04866976663470268},{"text":" ","start":0.3,"end":0.36,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.00001597391747054644},{"text":"dollar,","start":0.36,"end":0.72,"type":"word","logprob":-0.0006915231341346433},{"text":" ","start":0.72,"end":1.18,"type":"spacing","logprob":-7.629365427419543e-6},{"text":"doubling","start":1.18,"end":1.52,"type":"word","logprob":-7.629365427419543e-6},{"text":" ","start":1.52,"end":1.72,"type":"spacing","logprob":-4.768370445162873e-7},{"text":"every","start":1.74,"end":1.96,"type":"word","logprob":-4.768370445162873e-7},{"text":" ","start":1